Each `geom_*()` function adds a new layer to the plot, just like stacking transparent sheets on top of each other to build the final image.
:::

## Aesthetic Mappings {.smaller}

::: {.columns}
::: {.column}



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(
  data = iris,
  mapping = aes(
    x = Sepal.Length,
    y = Petal.Length
  )
) +
  geom_point(aes(color = Species)) +
  geom_smooth(method = "lm", se = FALSE)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](r_w05_slides_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-19-1.png){width=960}
:::
:::


:::
::: {.column .fragment}



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(
  data = iris,
  mapping = aes(
    x = Sepal.Length,
    y = Petal.Length,
    color = Species
  )
) +
  geom_point() +
  geom_smooth(method = "lm", se = FALSE)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](r_w05_slides_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-20-1.png){width=960}
